this morning on the dish a familiar face  in a new place chef alfred portale has  spent nearly four decades in the  culinary sphere  a pioneer in the new american food  movement with multiple james beard  awards a michelin star  unprecedented reviews and three  best-selling cookbooks portale has  little to prove  but that didn't stop him from leaving  the iconic new york restaurant he helped  build  to open a place of his own  with a new year's themed brunch as  inspiration we're going to taste  a pasta that we put together it's a  maine lobster it's got a little bit of  chervil and some salmon roll on top  barrow in an italian staple served with  walnut oil and wild mushrooms  rack of lamb with chicante beans some  braised escarole  shaved black truffle on here as well and  lastly for dessert a chocolate  and coffee tiramisu delicious chef  alfred portale  sat down to reflect so this is called a  spallata  it translates to a mistake and the story  goes the bartender was making a negroni  and he reached for the gin but he ended  up with some prosecco  a couple of parts campari and vermouth  and proseccos  cheers cheers to that i like mistakes  after more than three decades as  executive chef and partner of new york's  iconic  gotham bar and grill portale knows a  thing or two about mistakes  and even more about successes the james  beard award winner's latest venture is  also his first  solo endeavor his namesake portale  what is the pressure then like when you  say okay leaving that  i'm going to start this you didn't think  about that before you did it  i did think about it what did you want  that restaurant to be i wanted it to be  many things i wanted to be an expression  of myself i tried to create  a very chic and sort of sexy and fun  and lively place for the food he turned  to a combination of his personal  and culinary past both of my  grandparents  are from sicily actually but all my  training is french  sort of the bold passion of italy and  the precision of french cooking that's  how we  we look at it i guess italian food is in  your blood is that yes big italian  american family  lots of cousins my mother was an  excellent cook  her red sauce turned into your white  sauce  is that right oh that's funny my mom  used to make a big pot of red sauce with  the meatballs and brazil and all the  i carry on that tradition you know i've  tweaked them over the years  it's a white bolognese so made with  short rib and  some black truffle it's a nice dish my  whole career i've always  looked for classic dishes classic flavor  combinations  and tried to give it a personal touch  that kind of creative expression  part of what drew portale to cooking in  the first place  from early childhood i wanted to be an  artist you know it started with a next  door neighbor  who was a painter and used to give me  art lessons  when i was i must have been eight years  old nine years old  what did you love about it you know it's  just the creative  aspect of it being able to design and  express yourself that way  somehow i was turned on to cooking  through  some old french cookbooks that had  illustrations of these  big elaborate buffets that they used to  do in the 20s and 30s  and i said this is edible art which is  exactly what portale would go on to  create  building a following and reputation with  his masterpieces  at gotham bar and grill at portale his  creative touch  is still found in the architecture of  the food but also  in the space itself i had a great deal  to do with the design  the integration of art and music all  sort of with a postmodern  sort of vibe to it cooking is related to  art in some ways because  you know it's instant gratification so  you create a wonderful dish  and get it into production and serve it  to a guest  i mean i think that's the reward one  thing out of portale's control  timing his restaurant's launch was in  the fall of 2019  just a few months before the pandemic  began  could anything have prepared you for it  i don't even have to finish the question  yeah could anything have prepared you no  i mean  who could have ever conceived something  like this i mean  you know it's it's it's it's really  tough for for restaurants  um during this time for sure  i feel for my staff and everyone in the  industry that's been  impacted by this much of portale staff  is more like  family after so many years of working  together  and it was family he thought of when i  asked him our traditional dish question  if you could have this meal with anyone  past or present oh wow  who would it be you know we spoke about  her earlier and  i thought about her a lot i do miss my  mom  you know she was she was important did  she get to see a lot of your  success yeah they did actually you know  they  god blessed them they lived into their  90s but  yeah i came to new york came to gotham  on a number of occasions  but always kept me really well grounded  you know i'm like mom you know i'm on tv  i get it we just got three stars from  the new york times  you didn't call me last week right  something like that yeah something like  that  what would she think of the white sauce  oh god well  i think she'd be skeptical at first but  once she tasted it  maybe next i think i'd win it over  strong  and cheers to mom and the white sauce i  couldn't bring you food but i did make a  drink i don't know how i do as a  bartender but  was already drinking during the piece  [Music]  i saw it it's a wonderful mistake  that's all i know it's very strong and  portale is still doing an outdoor dining  program they're going right now  like all restaurants just trying to make  the best of it
 

